// @check
// @error this range never runs: `5 to 1` counts up (step 1) from a start above its end
// A provably-empty CONSTANT range is refused, not run: `5 to 1` counts up from a
// start above its end, so the body can never execute and the program says nothing
// about it. The TS core warned here; a warning is exactly what the reporter of
// D1588 would not have seen — `vl run` prints none and `vl check` exits 0 on one.
// Descending needs a negative step (`5 to 1 step -1`, which runs — for-step.vl).
let s = 0
for i in 5 to 1 {
  s = s + i
}
print(s)
